    {"id":"MPPSC-2012-031","paper_id":"MPPSC-2012-P1","exam":"MPPSC State Service Preliminary Examination","year":2012,"set_code":"A","question_number":31,"question_type":"statement_based",
     "language_variants":{"en":{"question_text":"Which one among the following is incorrect statement about the Constituent Assembly? (A) It worked with the help of a large number of committees, the most important among them being the Drafting Committee. (B) Minority communities like Christians, Anglo-Indians and Parsis were adequately represented in the Assembly. (C) It was elected on the basis of universal adult franchise. (D) Its electoral process was based on the sixth schedule of the Act of 1935 which allowed for a restricted franchise based on tax, property and educational qualification.","instructions":None,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"(A) only"},{"key":"B","text":"(B) only"},{"key":"C","text":"(C) only"},{"key":"D","text":"(D) only"}]},
                        "hi":{"question_text":"निम्नलिखित में से संविधान सभा के बारे में **गलत कथन कौनसा है** ? (A) इसने बड़ी संख्या में समितियों की मदद से काम किया। उनमें से प्रारूप समिति सबसे महत्वपूर्ण थी। (B) अल्पसंख्यक समुदाय जैसे ईसाई, एंग्लो-इंडियन और पारसियों को सभा में पर्याप्त प्रतिनिधित्व दिया गया। (C) इसका निर्वाचन सार्वभौम वयस्क मताधिकार के आधार पर किया गया। (D) इसकी चुनाव प्रक्रिया 1935 के अधिनियम के 6वें अनुसूची पर आधारित थी।","instructions":None,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"केवल (A)"},{"key":"B","text":"केवल (B)"},{"key":"C","text":"केवल (C)"},{"key":"D","text":"केवल (D)"}]}},
     "supplied_answer":{"answer":["C"],"status":"supplied","source":"Source material (no official key); independently verified.","notes":"Statement C claims universal adult franchise; the Constituent Assembly was elected by provincial legislatures (indirect election) with a restricted franchise, not universal adult franchise. So C is incorrect."},
     "answer_key_status":"supplied",
     "verified_answer":{"answer":["C"],"verified_by":"Pipeline independent verification","verified_at":"2026-11-02","evidence":[{"title":"Constituent Assembly — election method (indirect, restricted franchise)","citation":"Standard polity references / Constitution of India texts","url":"https://www.constitutionofindia.net/constitution_assembly_debates/"}],"status":"verified"},
     "explanation":{"language":"en","correct_reasoning":"Statement C is incorrect. The Constituent Assembly was NOT elected on the basis of universal adult franchise. It was elected by the members of the provincial legislative assemblies (indirect election), and the franchise was restricted under the provisions of the Government of India Act, 1935. Statement D describes this restriction correctly, making it the correct (true) statement. Since the question asks which statement is incorrect, the answer is C.","option_explanations":[{"key":"A","text":"(A) only","is_correct":False,"reason":"Statement A is correct: the Constituent Assembly worked through many committees, with the Drafting Committee being the most important."},{"key":"B","text":"(B) only","is_correct":False,"reason":"Statement B is correct: minority communities were given adequate representation in the Assembly."},{"key":"C","text":"(C) only","is_correct":True,"reason":"Correct. Statement C is incorrect because the Constituent Assembly was not elected by universal adult franchise but by provincial legislatures with a restricted franchise."},{"key":"D","text":"(D) only","is_correct":False,"reason":"Statement D is actually a correct description of the restricted franchise; it describes the process correctly."}],"key_concepts":["Constituent Assembly — elected indirectly by provincial legislatures (1935 Act, restricted franchise)","Universal adult franchise = direct election (not used for Constituent Assembly)"],"revision_takeaways":["Constituent Assembly = indirect election (provincial legislatures), restricted franchise, not universal adult franchise."],"sources":[{"title":"Constituent Assembly Debates","citation":"National Portal of India / Lok Sabha Secretariat","url":"https://www.constitutionofindia.net/constitution_assembly_debates/"}]},
     "subject":"Polity","topic":"Constitution of India","subtopic":"Making of the Constitution",
     "dispute":{"is_disputed":True,"status":"unresolved","reason":"The question asks for the 'incorrect statement'. Option C claims universal adult franchise, which is indeed incorrect. Option D describes the restricted franchise, which is a true statement. The answer is clearly C. No further ambiguity remains, but the dispute block documents the verification process.","raised_by":"Pipeline verification — statement-based question"},
     "source_reference":{"file":"/tmp/arena-coding-uploads/MPPSC-Prelims-Exam-Paper-2012-Paper-I.md","page":12,"question_location":"Q31","note":"Statement-based question. Note: the source has option C as 'universal adult franchise' which is historically incorrect."},
     "validation_status":"valid","validation_notes":["Unique ID MPPSC-2012-031.","No duplicate content detected.","Answer verified: C (Universal adult franchise — incorrect statement)."]},
